+      turns a hard finding into no finding, the epic owner refused to let it be
+      deferred, and `ProvenanceRecordExemptionTest` now pins it from four
+      directions with three separate disables (vacuity rows E, F, G) proving
+      each case reddens. What is STILL uncovered directly is
+      `HomeCloner.rootSpellings` and `insideHomeText`: both are exercised only
+      through `home verify`, which is behavioural coverage rather than a unit
+      test, and `insideHomeText` -- the cold-shim token substitution -- has no
+      assertion at all over its multi-spelling, longest-first replacement.
+
+      LOW-12, no size cap on the record read (every other whole-file read in
+      HomeCloner caps at WHOLE_FILE_LIMIT), and `HomeCloner.unsanctionedForeignHome`
+      builds a fresh cache map per call, so the pruner re-derives the chain once
+      per shim instead of once per foreign home.
+
+      LOW-13, `--strict` does not escalate the exemption. Every other tolerated
+      class (CONTENT_REFERENCE, DIAGNOSTIC_TEXT) becomes a failure under
+      --strict; the provenance exemption is silent at every strictness. Decide
+      deliberately and write down which.
+    reproduction: >
+      MED-3: truncate <home>/home.provenance.json to half its bytes, run sync,
+      watch the inherited shims be pruned with no diagnostic about the record.
+      MED-5: replace the record with a symlink to a file outside the home.
+    why_deferred: >
+      All six are hardening of a mechanism whose CORRECTNESS this ticket had to
+      establish first, and the review's two REQUIRED changes (re-derive rather
