+  found_by: 'HIS-7''s adversarial review (findings HIGH-3, MED-4, MED-6, MED-7), then MEASURED end to
+    end on 2026-08-21 against epic tip 23e35c7. Evidence in results/epic-home-integrity-sync/probes/his-10/.
+
+    '
+  root_cause: "A CLONE IS A GRANDCHILD THAT RECORDS NOTHING ABOUT ITS DESCENT.\nThe project home is a\
+    \ REGISTERED CHILD of root: root holds child-homes/<id>/child-home.json, so ChildHomeLink.isChildOf\
+    \ can answer yes and the five bin/cli symlinks into root are sanctioned parent-store shims. A worktree\
+    \ home is a COPY of the project home. Nothing in the copy records that it descends from a home whose\
+    \ parent is root. So every reader that needs \"is this foreign path sanctioned\" has to guess, and\
+    \ they guess differently:\n\n  home clone            clean -- \"no path in it reaches another home\"\
+    \n  home verify           exit 1 -- 5x FOREIGN_HOME\n  home verify --against exit 0 -- \"5 sanctioned\
+    \ parent-store shim(s)\"\n  sync                  PRUNES all five, \"not this home's parent store\"\
+    ,\n                        then spends ~90s re-provisioning five toolchains\n\nFour readers, three\
+    \ answers, one home, same five paths. The only thing that makes the sanction visible is an operator\
+    \ typing --against, which is a flag, not a fact.\nTHE SYNC BEHAVIOUR IS THE EXPENSIVE ONE and it contradicts\
+    \ the contract the owner stated for HIS-7: \"we clone, then we say, here are the artifacts for these\
+    \ skills on the path for you, and here is how you rebuild them if you make a change. Why would we\
+    \ build them without the agent changing?\" Today every worktree rebuilds five toolchains nobody touched,\
+    \ on its first sync, silently.\nSECOND HALF, #206: the verdict is not even spelling-invariant. HomeCloner.verifyRoots\
+    \ resolves the destination root (`realOrSame(dstRoot)` at :1635) for the symlink branch but hands\
+    \ the UNRESOLVED spelling to the provisioned-file branch (`missingReferencesIn(file, dstRoot)` at\
+    \ :1691), and destReferences (:1428) does a raw `text.indexOf(dstRoot.toString())`. Where the home\
+    \ is reached through a symlink, that branch reports clean WITHOUT HAVING CHECKED. CliArtifact.usableInHome\
+    \ does the same string walk.\nMEASURED 2026-08-21, and the obvious fixture is VACUOUS -- see results/epic-home-integrity-sync/probes/his-10/path-spelling.md.\
+    \ The macOS temp case does NOT trigger it: \"/private/var/X\" CONTAINS the substring \"/var/X\", so\
+    \ indexOf accidentally matches and the reference IS found. 24 of 29 registered graphs wire HomeFixpointLaw\
+    \ and every test-graph home lives under /var/folders/.../T; they are saved by that accident, not by\
+    \ correctness. The defect bites only where the two spellings are not substring-compatible -- a symlinked\
+    \ intermediate directory, a symlinked $HOME or checkout, /Volumes/..., a symlinked worktree path:\n\
+    \n  --home <s>/link/homeC     -> \"every reference ... resolves\"       BLIND\n  --home <s>/realdir/homeC\
+    \  -> \"1 reference(s) ... do not resolve\"  CORRECT\n\none home, one broken file, two spellings.\
+    \ A fixture built on /var or /tmp would pass before AND after the fix, which would have been this\
+    \ epic's THIRD vacuous assertion.\n"
+  slice: '(1) PROVENANCE. A clone records its descent durably -- what it was cloned from, and what that
+    home''s parent store is -- so the sanction is a fact in the copy rather than a flag on the command
+    line. Every reader answers from that one record. (2) SPELLING. Resolve the home root ONCE and hand
+    the same spelling to every branch, in HomeCloner.verifyRoots and CliArtifact.usableInHome. (3) THE
+    PRUNER. CliShimPruner stops deleting an inherited shim that the provenance record sanctions. The clone
+    keeps it on PATH and DECLARES it, per the lazy contract. NOT IN SCOPE: the write-confinement guard
+    (HIS-9), and repairing homes already pruned (HIS-13).
+
+    '
+  acceptance:
+    assertions:
+    - All four readers give the SAME verdict on one cloned home, with no --against flag.
+    - A clone's first sync leaves its inherited parent-store shims in place, and provisions nothing that
+      was already provided.
+    - The reader-agreement assertion FAILS when the provenance record is removed -- vacuity checked, in
+      writing.
+    - A home reached through a symlinked path verifies identically to the same home reached through its
+      real path, and that assertion fails when the resolution is removed.
+    - 'A copy of an UNSANCTIONED home is still unsanctioned: cloning is not a laundering step. The existing
+      HomeCloner guard for this must still pass.'
+    - '`--against` no longer decides the answer; it may still explain it.'
+  goals:
+  - goal: GOAL-one-home-one-answer
+    contribution: direct
+    expected_effect: four readers, three answers -> four readers, one answer, and spelling-invariant
+    local_signal: python skills/test_graph/scripts/run.py home-integrity
+  - goal: GOAL-home-invariants
+    contribution: direct
+    expected_effect: an invariant that a home's sanction set is a function of its recorded descent, not
+      of the command line
+    local_signal: jbang RunTests.java
+- id: HIS-11
+  title: compensation for CommitUnitsToStore is delete-only, so a failed install destroys the bytes it
+    overwrote
+  phase: HIS
+  status: planned
+  epic: home-integrity-sync
+  github_issue: 186
+  added_in_schedule_revision: 4
